    description: "[REVIEW 2026-11-01, PARTLY-STALE] Reviewed 2026-11-01 at 100b6fbb6e: NewType has 0 uses in packages/*/src. INV-lidul was satisfied 2026-06-17 via fingerprint stamping (PR #271), not NewType, and compute_config_fingerprint({}) still returns sha256:44136fa355b3678a (no refusing factory). INV-kurup's Symbol.id/Edge.id bypasses now have a static lint (scripts/check-id-construction, WI-vodin, in pre-commit). The INV-lidul rationale is void; re-scope to fields that lint does not cover. (Original text below; the review entry in the thread has the evidence.)\n\nIntroduce NewType aliases for identifier-bearing fields: StableId, NodeId, EdgeId, ConfigFingerprint, etc. Pair each with a canonical factory function (compute_stable_id, make_node_id, etc.) that's the only entry point for constructing the NewType. Refactor emitters that currently use raw str for these fields. Closes some INV-kurup canonical-factory-bypass sub-cases at type-check time — direct str → NewType assignment becomes a type error, forcing the call site through the factory. Also closes part of INV-lidul (config_fingerprint constant) — the factory can refuse to construct a fingerprint from an empty config dict."  # 238b
